From b2987ba485628078ff4a27a114488912631d65fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:45:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] NV0039 memory-to-memory copies on subchannel 1
 (PS3RECOMP_NV0039), coherent with the draw engine's surfaces

Killzone HD's MLAA (FUN_001109E8) copies the finished frame from the display
buffer to a 1280x720 image in main memory with NV0039 and the previous one,
which its SPU post chain processed (MLAA, glow, motion blur), back. The title
binds NV4097 to subchannel 1 as well, so the walker sends that subchannel to
the 3D engine and the copies were dropped. A transfer is told apart by its
shape (0x184/0x188 with two 0xFEED000x handles, then 0x30C..0x328 as one run
of 8); the source rows are read back from an engine surface first and the
destination rows uploaded after. Off by default.

